    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.operators\n\n### Question\n\n`v_P` is quite a new addition to Vim related to the idea of a `replace-with-register`-operator\r\n\r\ne.g. oldest `replace` plugin I know (which I used before mini.operators):\r\nhttps://github.com/inkarkat/vim-replacewithregister\r\n\r\nDiscussion when `v_P` was added:\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/g/vim_dev/c/H_HzHcGXNxA\r\n\r\nWhen it was added, I was wondering whether it makes a visual mode replace operator redundant:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/inkarkat/vim-ReplaceWithRegister/issues/6\r\n\r\nHow about in mini.operators, are there any differences with `v_P` and `v_gr` (however small)?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.operators</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">v_P</code> is quite a new addition to Vim related to the idea of a <code class=\"notranslate\">replace-with-register</code>-operator</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">e.g. oldest <code class=\"notranslate\">replace</code> plugin I know (which I used before mini.operators):<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/inkarkat/vim-replacewithregister\">https://github.com/inkarkat/vim-replacewithregister</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Discussion when <code class=\"notranslate\">v_P</code> was added:<br>\n<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/g/vim_dev/c/H_HzHcGXNxA\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://groups.google.com/g/vim_dev/c/H_HzHcGXNxA</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When it was added, I was wondering whether it makes a visual mode replace operator redundant:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1883163330\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/inkarkat/vim-ReplaceWithRegister/issues/6\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/inkarkat/vim-ReplaceWithRegister/issues/6/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/inkarkat/vim-ReplaceWithRegister/issues/6\">inkarkat/vim-ReplaceWithRegister#6</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How about in mini.operators, are there any differences with <code class=\"notranslate\">v_P</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">v_gr</code> (however small)?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.operators\nQuestion\nv_P is quite a new addition to Vim related to the idea of a replace-with-register-operator\ne.g. oldest replace plugin I know (which I used before mini.operators):\nhttps://github.com/inkarkat/vim-replacewithregister\nDiscussion when v_P was added:\nhttps://groups.google.com/g/vim_dev/c/H_HzHcGXNxA\nWhen it was added, I was wondering whether it makes a visual mode replace operator redundant:\ninkarkat/vim-ReplaceWithRegister#6\nHow about in mini.operators, are there any differences with v_P and v_gr (however small)?",
    "category": {
